READING
============================================================================
  The index-only walk dies at the SEED, not in the graph. The hop-0 lookup is
  an exact normalized match on "rel of subj": when the parse is wrong, or the
  phrasing merely differs, there is nothing to start from — and no amount of
  backward traversal helps, because there is no frontier to traverse from.

  This is why the decomposition's cosine backward probe found 43 and an exact
  index lookup finds ~2: the 43 came from FUZZY matching on object text.

  So wiring `by_object` into the walk is NOT the free win it looks like, and
  the index cannot stand in for the retriever. It serves only hops whose
  surface form already matches. The knowledge is largely present — the gold
  answer is an entity in a 78%-complete index for half of these failures —
  but there is no way in.

  THE RETRIEVER'S JOB, as specified by this measurement:
    1. hop-0 ENTRY is the product. 61% of surviving failures never get a seed.
       Later-hop traversal is comparatively healthy and the index already does it.
    2. It must be fuzzy on the tail, where the question's surface form and the
       fact's differ. Exact match is what is failing.
    3. Bidirectional edges are worth ~nothing on exact match (+2) but `by_object`
       is already built and costs nothing — wire it once fuzzy seeding lands.
